Version: 0.0.7.9000
Date: 2026-09-21
R: 4.4.3
Studies: coverage, power, mclogit, bench, brms, imputation, messy
Date.messy: 2026-09-22
Note: A COMPLETE retention set. All five standing studies were re-run at this
 version alongside the new imputation ablation, at the same parameters as
 0.0.2.9000 so the two are directly comparable: coverage and power 2000
 replicates, mclogit 500, bench 160, brms 3. Every cell that existed at
 0.0.2.9000 reproduces it.
Note: The coverage study grew from 23 cells to 32. Everything added between
 0.0.3.9000 and 0.0.7.9000 had agreement against an outside implementation
 but no coverage of its own, and those are different claims: agreement says
 the point estimate is right, coverage says the interval is. New cells:
 zero-inflated Poisson (mixed) and hurdle Poisson, ordered logit fixed and
 mixed, beta and zero-inflated beta, two-stage least squares, a stratified
 clustered weighted sample, and a mediation ACME.
Note: Two of the new cells are not at nominal and both are reported rather
 than smoothed over. `mediate` OVER-covers at 0.967 with a standard-error
 ratio of 1.107: the ACME interval is a percentile interval from simulation
 draws and comes out about 11% wider than the sampling variability of the
 estimate, which is conservative rather than wrong. `svy_strat` covers at
 0.939 with a ratio of 0.956; at 2000 replicates the Monte Carlo error is
 0.005, so that is about two standard errors below nominal -- small, real,
 and in the anti-conservative direction, which is the one that matters.
Note: The imputation ablation was built to settle whether ilm_lowrank_ncp()
 picks a poor rank, which a single earlier design had suggested. It does not
 settle it: cross-validation is worse than parallel analysis in four cells
 and materially better in one. The selector is unchanged. See
 studies/findings/imputation.md.
Note: Chained equations cannot be fitted at n = 60, p = 80 and does not fail
 fast when asked -- it runs for hours on rank-deficient per-column
 regressions. That cell is recorded as inapplicable rather than attempted.
Note: Everything here was fitted by maximum likelihood. REML arrived at this
 version but is opt-in for ilm_model(), so the defaults these studies
 exercise are unchanged, and the numbers remain comparable with 0.0.2.9000.
Note: The messy-data comparison (messy) was run a day after the rest of the
 set, on 2026-09-22, at 400 replicates per regime, which is why it carries a
 date of its own. It was first written to runs/messy/ and moved here, to the
 layout the summariser and the pruner expect; its findings have been
 generated by summarise_run.R since. It counted an illume fit usable only
 with nlminb code 0 AND a positive definite Hessian. Fixed effects at a
 variance boundary have since been reported rather than refused, which on the
 same seeds raises the usable share with a true SD of 0.05 from 63.3% to
 97.5% (see NEWS); the numbers recorded here are the ones measured at the time.
